  Preheat a #yogurt maker{} or #slow cooker{} on Low according to manufacturer's instructions.

Whisk @milk{4%cups} and @instant nonfat dry milk powder{0.25%cup} together in a #saucepan{} over medium heat until almost boiling, ~{4%minutes}. Cool until lukewarm (100 to 110 degrees F/38 to 45 degrees C).

Gently stir @plain kefir{0.5%cup} into milk mixture until just combined; pour into #yogurt containers{} or #jars{} with airtight lids. Add to yogurt maker or slow cooker.

Cook on Low until desired level of tartness and consistency is reached, ~{4-10%hours}. Chill yogurt in the #refrigerator{} at least ~{2%hours} before serving.